    "verdict": "ACCEPT corrected source documentation; runtime HOLD",
    "text": "# Tooltip window 2 closure review\n\nDecision: ACCEPT the corrected finite source findings for documentation. Runtime implementation remains HOLD. Review performed on 2026-10-09 against research commit `13311c8b3afe961dd4ca25d9ba3c70d19551c82f` and explicit application main `47680b8fd124aab50b0528eea77a81cacb556060`.\n\nAccepted artifact: `issue19-tooltip-controller-source-20261009/work/orchestration/tooltip-window2-closure-20261009-1257/closure-addendum-corrected.md`, SHA256 `b290c6de17e3e38a53f26ad10f35a80cd71593023859ebe41b9a8a1741e55a8f`; corrected receipt SHA256 `ef76c10bf33e9531fa80d593f1831572b6e96fc1bfeed70c8a842b7cba135cdb`. Original addendum `339acc09eb1e925edda9f621fbd9baeb1377798c12120f92f716d1bb7164581f` and receipt `0e0ea53ece43db7afd5998ef54001a3e6df6f929d93fe98dde042b901c052bb9` are preserved unchanged.\n\nIndependent readback verified 27 source hashes against the named commits/current files, all 15 original artifact hashes/sizes, and 1,234 disassembly byte lines across ten retained windows against the inert PE. This count includes padding and the explicitly superseded discovery window; it is byte correspondence, not executed coverage. The 12 literal-address contexts, six direct getter calls and four input jump-table entries also match the original bytes. Original EXE SHA256 remains `3a5065c7420b3fcde208bf220bc86dfbac95e025ab2492caf9c7ea5308dfbe4f`. The research checkout was clean. No original, application, browser or test execution was performed for this review.\n\nThe material findings are supported:\n\n- `004513d0` returns signed word `0089ce7a`. The window presenter resets it to -1 and its hit-test producers publish indices 0\u20136. It denotes the last-painted control index. It is not an active-window identity. Half-open control rectangles remain distinct from case ba's inclusive window rectangle.\n- `0045e730` compares the old and new index and increments the separate word `0089ce7e` only when equal and different from -1; otherwise it resets that counter. This does not supply tooltip dwell `0068c6af`. The generic renderer has its own retained conditional counter handling and is not claimed equivalent in every branch.\n- Already-enabled window 2 can re-enter enable when the retained index is -1. The retained unconditional saved-mode writes then permit saving mode 17 over the earlier mode. A universal promise to restore the first pre-window mode would alter this behavior.\n- The presenter directly owns record 2 geometry and its illustration call. It clears only words at slot offsets +0/+2/+4/+6/+0xa and flag bits 0x3c at +0xf across 32 slots. The corrected text no longer claims whole-slot zeroing.\n- `0045ea00` tests widget/control results against -1, without a signed nonnegative guard. The corrected text preserves that exact predicate and does not infer the unexpanded widget helper's return domain. Its action table supports the stated scroll, history-call and close routing. Caller eligibility and earlier input interception remain relevant.\n\nThe eight-row prerequisite table is an accurate separation of retained native findings and missing port ownership. It preserves shared dwell/history, fresh inspection-record acceleration, forced precedence, five-owner cleanup uncertainty, and the absence of a fixed-Hz substitution. No independently complete playable tooltip slice is established by this pass.\n\nThe smallest named next source prerequisite for the included contextual window is the two direct local text/layout consumers `0045d8c0` and `0045dcb0`. Literal title/label data and full widget semantics are not recovered here; \u201ccontextual help\u201d remains inference. Their absence is a local source boundary, not a demonstrated missing external input. Other rows' explicitly named owner/guard mappings remain required only as the admitted complete interaction scope demands. This verdict authorizes preservation of these source findings, not application changes or expanded research.\n"
